  "description": "<strong>🎵 </strong><em>This experience is brought to you by </em><strong><em>City Music Promotions</em></strong><em>. </em><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Tickets for Grieg Piano Concerto and the Northern Lights at St Paul's Church, Covent Garden</strong><br>\r\n🎫 Band AA Ticket (Front Section)<br>\r\n🎫 Band A Ticket<br>\r\n🎫 Band B Ticket<br>\r\n🎫 Band C Ticket<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<em>Upon arrival, you will be assigned a seat within the pre-reserved band. We recommend arriving as early as possible.</em><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Highlights</strong><br>\r\n🎼 Enjoy Grieg's much-loved piano concerto and other masterpieces<br>\r\n🎻 Stunning performances from the highly acclaimed musicians of the Piccadilly Sinfonietta<br>\r\n⭐ The perfect option for first-time classical concert-goers<br>\r\n⛪ The beautiful candlelit St Paul's Church with an additional light show to enhance the experience further<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>General Info</strong><br>\r\n📅 <strong>Dates and times:</strong> select your dates/times directly in the ticket selector<br>\r\n⏳ <strong>Concert Duration:</strong> 1 hour (Doors open 20 minutes before start time)<br>\r\n📍<strong> Location:</strong> St Paul's Church, Covent Garden, London<br>\r\n👤 <strong>Age requirement:</strong> CityMusic Promotions events are not suitable for children under the age of 5 years old (babies will not be admitted)<br>\r\n🎵 Genre: classical music<br>\r\n❗ Important: all sales are final, and tickets cannot be refunded, changed, or modified<br>\r\n📝 Please note: arrive early, as seats are assigned within your pre-reserved band upon arrival\r\n<p></p>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Concert Details</strong><br>\r\n<br>\r\nExperience an unforgettable musical evening as the<strong> Piccadilly Sinfonietta</strong> perform a dazzling programme of classical masterpieces in the stunning candlelit setting of<strong> St Paul’s Covent Garden — the Actors’ Church</strong>. Surrounded by the vibrant atmosphere of Covent Garden, this enchanting concert offers the perfect way to spend an elegant evening in the heart of London. The concert includes a specially designed lighting experience to perfectly compliment the programme with a 'Northern Lights' theme.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nFrom the serene beauty of Elgar’s Serenade for Strings to the thrilling energy of Grieg’s In the Hall of the Mountain King, this carefully curated programme showcases some of the most evocative and beloved works in the orchestral repertoire. The concert also features the radiant Morning from Peer Gynt, Elgar’s deeply moving Nimrod from the Enigma Variations, and Grieg’s magnificent Piano Concerto in A minor performed by <strong>renowned concert pianist Warren Mailley-Smith</strong>.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nPerformed by the acclaimed Piccadilly Sinfonietta, this captivating programme promises an evening of musical brilliance, passion and atmosphere in one of London’s most unique and historic venues.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Featuring</strong><br>\r\nThe Piccadilly Sinfonietta<br>\r\nWarren Mailley-Smith (Piano)<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Programme</strong><br>\r\nElgar – <em>Serenade for Strings</em><br>\r\nGrieg – <em>In the Hall of the Mountain King</em><br>\r\nGrieg –<em> Morning from Peer Gynt</em><br>\r\nElgar – <em>Nimrod (from the Enigma Variations)</em><br>\r\nGrieg – <em>Piano Concerto in A minor</em><br>\r\n<br>\r\nSince its founding in 2017, The Piccadilly Sinfonietta has captivated audiences across the UK, performing over 200 concerts annually in many of the country’s most prestigious venues. Featuring virtuosic soloists and extraordinary musicianship, the ensemble is renowned for its dynamic performances and its ability to bring classical music to life with flair, passion and finesse.",
